  "user_id": 1574,
  "properties": {
    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "## **Dropdown Search**\r\n\r\n### Do This:\r\n\r\n1. In `prompt.md`, plan how you want your search to work.\r\n\r\n2. Give your plan to AI and ask it to help you write the `subjectSearch()` function.\r\n\r\n3. Your function should:\r\n\r\n   * get the selected value from the dropdown using `.value`\r\n   * reset `displayResources` to an empty array\r\n   * use `.map()` to go through each resource in `resources`\r\n   * use an `if` statement to decide which resources should be kept\r\n   * add matching resources to `displayResources`\r\n   * call `renderResources()` at the end\r\n\r\n4. Complete the `clearSearch()` function so it:\r\n\r\n   * sets the dropdown value back to `\"All\"` using `.value`\r\n   * shows all resources again\r\n\r\n5. Ask AI to suggest test cases to check your search. Try those tests in the app.",
    "submittable": "false",
    "disable_edit_run_for_submission": "false",
    "hide_share_and_remix": "false",
    "widget_view": "false",
    "initial_view_mode": "split",
    "ai_tutor_mode": "engineer",
    "predict_settings": {
